    "rationale": "Audited registered policy workflow.planning.lifecycle-authority in exact proposal revision13906993f25ac027f2a6be4e9a9aac531b30bad56d3acbb64afa163ab093737a against accepted base daa70d98328a88b125dd9df3f896a0502e8233b7. Current actual semantic consumers within audit-horizon.policy-impact-consumers are: planning-consolidation (enforcement-suite-projection); profile.workflow.concurrent-plan-integration (normative-consumer); workflow.implementation (normative-consumer); workflow.planning.discovery (normative-consumer); prompts/implement-plan.md (prompt-projection); prompts/planning.md (prompt-projection); templates/PLAN-TEMPLATE.md (template-projection). Inspected the owner and declared consumer scopes, incoming/outgoing graph, relevant canonical references, registered prompts/templates, affected fixtures/suite contracts and generic implementations. Independent Standards/Spec review confirmed exact unchanged normative text after the13 required consumer declarations were added; handoff, lifecycle/isolation and opening-phase omissions are resolved. The paired30 consumer reviews and exact candidate application read/route observations establish that every identified material consumer within these18 registered-unit scopes has a disposition and no known actual relationship remains undeclared. Pinned unchanged tracked evidence supports consumer ownership/representation and enforcement limits and is verified byte-identical to the captured accepted base. This completeness conclusion covers the identified semantic consumer inventory, not conversational inference, agent effectiveness, execution of all consumer code or library-wide completeness. Planning's unregistered Acceptance Claims, Concurrent Work, Artifact Model and Concurrent Integration Routing remain outside this registered-unit audit and retain their normative force. Conditional links to Architecture/CodeDesign/Contracts do not themselves declare projected tests; the preexisting unreviewed concurrent-integration profile exposure is unchanged. Standards Authoring's referenced review/publication and downstream-evidence rules support these explicit limits.",
